    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as the clear offensive engine. His score of 80.98 is the highest on the board, driven by a favorable matchup against L\u00f3pez (4.33 xERA) and the premium value we assign to his leadoff spot and elite stolen base upside. Similarly, **Lars Nootbaar** projects strongly (65.16) from the leadoff spot; while he faces the formidable Sandy Alcantara, his dynamic platoon advantage against a right-handed arm and the inherent efficiency of the #1 order spot keep him locked into a high-floor role. **Colt Keith** (60.15) and **Carson Benge** (61.13) also provide solid utility, with both benefiting from advantageous lineup placement in the 3 and 4 holes, respectively, against favorable right-handed starters.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card was leaving **Chase Meidroth** on the bench. With a score of 33.18, he fell well below our 40-point \"Zebras Floor.\" While he is a capable asset, his matchup against Williams (2.89 xERA) presented too much risk to his efficiency, specifically in the batting average category where a high-skill arm like Williams tends to suppress production. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Dillon Dingler** (42.89). His score is propped up by his batting order, but the dynamic platoon penalty against Soriano serves as a warning that his plate appearances may be less productive than his raw base projection suggests. With **Yordan Alvarez**, **Trea Turner**, and **Junior Caminero** all sidelined due to scheduling, the onus is on our active starters to maintain our category standings without relying on the top-tier ceiling these rested stars usually provide.",
